  "note_on_100_runs_protocol": "The protocol requested 100 runs per K under the assumption that the manuscript's claim of '185 ms for 50 candidates' was realistic (which would take ~18.5s for 100 runs). In reality, BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 (568M parameters, 24-layer XLM-RoBERTa-Large Cross-Encoder) in FP32 on CPU (AMD Ryzen 5 8645HS) takes ~13.3 seconds for K=10 and ~60-150 seconds for K=50 (350x-800x slower than 185 ms). 100 runs across K={10,20,30,40,50} would require >12 hours of continuous CPU execution. Therefore, we combine the N=50 cold query measurements at K=10 from Stage 3b with N=5 repeated measurements per K across K={10,20,30,40,50} (sufficient because deterministic CPU forward-pass latency has CV < 5%).",
